# Legacy HPC Projects — Static Archive

This repository contains:

✅ A Python crawler to extract HPC project pages  
✅ A static archive of HTML pages  
✅ A GitHub Pages site to browse the archive  

---

# 🌐 Public website

👉 https://un-ocha.github.io/legacy-hpc-projects/

Example:

👉 https://un-ocha.github.io/legacy-hpc-projects/projects/229791.html

---

# 🧠 Overview

This project generates a static archive of HPC project pages.

The workflow is:

Crawler → generate HTML → save to docs/ → git push → GitHub Pages updates

GitHub Pages serves content from the repository automatically after each push.

---

# 📁 Output structure

legacy-hpc-projects/

├── docs/                      ← ✅ PUBLISHED WEBSITE (GitHub Pages)
│   ├── index.html
│   ├── projects/
│   └── _assets/
│
├── output/                    ← local temporary output (NOT in repository)
│   ├── json/
│   ├── screenshots/
│   ├── debug/
│   └── crawler.log
│
├── html_crawler.py            ← ✅ MAIN crawler
├── requirements.txt
├── input_projects_*.csv
└── README.md

👉 Only the `/docs` folder is published.

# ⚙️ Initial setup (one-time)

## ✅ 1. Clone the repository

```
bash
git clone https://github.com/UN-OCHA/legacy-hpc-projects.git
cd legacy-hpc-projects
```

***

## ✅ 2. Install dependencies

```
bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
playwright install
```

***

## ✅ 3. First-time setup

Before running the crawler for the first time, you must run:

```
bash
git push --set-upstream origin main
```

***

## ✅ 3. Configure crawler output

The crawler is already configured to write directly to `docs/projects/`.
Only modify this if you change the project structure.

***

# ▶️ Running the crawler

```
bash
python html_crawler.py
```

This will generate files like:

docs/projects/229791.html
docs/projects/229790.html
...

***

# 💾 Publishing changes


The crawler automatically commits and pushes updates to GitHub.

During execution:
- HTML files are written to `docs/`
- Git commits are created in batches
- Changes are pushed automatically

No manual `git add / commit / push` is required.

---

## Manual push (optional)

If needed, you can still run:

```
bash
git add docs/
git commit -m "Manual update"
git push
```

***

## ✅ Deployment

GitHub Pages automatically publishes updates.

⏱ Typical delay: 1–2 minutes

***

# ⚠️ Important notes

* GitHub Pages is configured to serve from `/docs`
* `index.html` must exist in `/docs`
* Paths are case-sensitive
* Only static files are supported (HTML, CSS, JS, images)
* A `.nojekyll` file is included to ensure GitHub Pages does not ignore `_assets/` folders
* The first push may take longer if many HTML files are generated

***

# 🧪 Troubleshooting

## ❌ Site not updating

* Wait 1–2 minutes
* Check repository → Settings → Pages

## ❌ 404 errors

* Ensure files exist in `docs/projects/`
* Check filename casing

## ❌ Missing styles/assets

* Ensure `_assets/` is inside `/docs`

***

# ✅ Summary

Crawler → docs/projects → git commit → git push → GitHub Pages → live website

